# core/tests/talk_gen/mem.tlk - the talk memory probes (test_talk_save.c, T6). Not game
# text. Compiled into TALK_gentest.BIN after gentest.tlk; each rule answers an act that
# gentest.tlk has no rule for, so a test picks it by the act.
@rule core.promise act: tease
  "You promised last time." guard: fact.promised
  "A first promise." guard: !fact.promised
@rule core.apologize act: complain
  "Still cross about last time." guard: fact.insulted
  "Sorry for what?" guard: !fact.insulted
@rule core.offer act: thank
  "You were kind last time." guard: fact.complimented
  "Oh, thanks." guard: !fact.complimented
@rule core.ask_advice act: answer
  "Last time: {mem}." guard: fact.memory
  "Nothing yet." guard: !fact.memory
@rule cb.memory
  "Again {mem}." guard: fact.memory
